   },
   "evidence": "The injected GitHub lookup demonstrated that probe count grows directly with historical collisions, without a candidate cap. Each iteration creates a fresh retry budget through withGitHubRetry or remoteSh, and the loop runs inside withRepoLock. Base uses a run-specific branch and has no collision-probing loop. The claim overstates two details: lookup failures already propagate rather than advancing suffixes indefinitely, and rebuilding only the cache does not remove stored branch records, which short-circuit remote probes. No real GitHub latency was measured; the problematic case requires a large collision history absent from both records and refs."
  }
